  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Dilip Ramchandra Maske vs The State Of Maharashtra on 23 March, 2023 Author: Anuja Prabhudessai Bench: Anuja Prabhudessai 7 aba 855-23.do In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 855 Of 2023 Dilip Ramchandra Maske ..Applicant v/s. The State of Maharashtra . ..Respondent Mr. Abhishek Nandinath i/b. Umesh R. Mankapure for the Applicant. Mr. Shrikant Yadav, App for the State. Coram : Anuja Prabhudessai ,J. Dated : 23rd March, 2023.",
    "facts": "3. The aforesaid crime was registered pursuant to the FIR lodged by Assistant Commissioner Umesh Subhash Bhuse. The case of the pps 1 of 3 7 aba 855-23.doc prosecution is that one vehicle bearing No. MH 45 AM 3771 was intercepted, and upon taking search of the said vehicle, it was revealed that the said vehicle was used to transport Gutkha pan masala from Karnataka to Mahrashtra. It is alleged that the driver of the said vehicle had disclosed that the Applicant is the owner of the gutkha which was being transported by the said vehicle. Learned APP states that the vehicle which was intercepted is registered in the name of the Applicant. This is a pre-arrest bail in connection with FIR No.155 of 2023 reg Mangalveda Police Station, Solapur for the offenses under 188, 272, 273, 328 of Indian Penal Code, 1860 ('IPC', for Section 26(2)(i), (ii), (iv), 27(3)(e), 30(2)(a), 59 of F Standards Act, 2006. allegation against the Applicant is that Pan Masala and G being carried / taken for the Applicant and FIR was regis statement of the driver of the vehicle involved. It is submitted that statements of the complainant, panchas, witnesses and Inventing Officer are recorded. It is informed that RCC No.482 of 2023 is registered in the concerned Court at Mangalwedha. No grievance is made about the Applicant's co-operation with investigation.",
    "arguments": "",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
